//! Bond-valence tables of CrysFML, the crystallographic library of FullProf and of its program Bond_Str: d0 and B0
//! of s = exp((d0 − d)/B0) for 247 cations with 14 anions, with their references; the anions' ionic radii; the
//! cations' ionic radii by oxidation state (Bond_Str counts a bond when d ≤ (r_cation + r_anion)(1 + tol)).
//!
//! Source: CrysFML (J. Rodríguez-Carvajal, J. González-Platas, N. A. Katcho, ILL; LGPL-3), the PyPI package crysfml
//! 0.8.0, `Src/CFML_Tables/Tab_Set_BVST.f90` (`BVS_Table`), `Src/CFML_BVS_Tables.f90` (`BVS_Anions`,
//! `BVS_Anions_Rion`, `REF_BVS`) and `Src/CFML_Tables/Tab_Set_ScatterT.f90` (`Chem_Info`: `Oxid`, `Rion`); written by
//! `core/tests/data/make_bv_table.py`. Do not edit. The test `bond_valence` checks them against Bond_Str's outputs.
// Table values are data, not approximations of mathematical constants.
#![allow(clippy::approx_constant)]

